{
  "accuracy_contract": {
    "combined": "The combined pane shows a conservative pixel-domain union of VLMaxxing fresh regions and RLT representative-token regions. It visualizes complementarity and possible composition, not an already-measured union runtime.",
    "denominators": "Overlay fractions are active-crop pixel fractions for visualization. The manifest records the RLT token-domain keep rate separately.",
    "measured_result_context": "The HUD's measured speedups and scorer-cost ratios come from RLT-as-C-VISION benchmark artifacts. They contextualize the visual intuition, but the overlay masks themselves are not exact replays of the Gemma runtime C-VISION masks.",
    "rlt": "RLT panes are computed with codec_through.rlt_masks on the same square-padded frames, using tau=0.1, tubelet_size=2, 224x224 ImageNet-normalized input, and patch_size=16. The visualization shows the thresholded RLT keep mask, mask only, no length encoding.",
    "rlt_frame_parity": "Displayed frame counts match the existing VLMaxxing windows. If a window has an odd frame count, the renderer duplicates the final frame only for RLT mask computation, then displays the original frame sequence.",
    "vlmaxxing": "Fresh/reuse boxes are recomputed with the existing Fig. 1 Qwen routing-budget policy, not hand annotated. This pane visualizes the VLMaxxing routing intuition, not the Gemma sparse-vision runtime mask."
  },
